<v Na Dortch>[CHEERING]
<v Na Dortch>昨天，我在家里，我就躺在床上。我想，哇。我真的他妈做到了。黑人，酷儿，牙齿坏了，有点胖——就像，妈的，我真的做到了。你知道我的意思吗？这感觉就像胜算对我不利。但我喜欢赢。我喜欢赢。

00:57:23.340 --> 00:57:28.450
<v Na Dortch>I'll try not to cry. I'm black and I'm proud!
<v Na Dortch>达娜·奇维斯（Dana Chivvis）是我们节目的制片人之一。

00:57:28.450 --> 00:57:41.120
<v Na Dortch>[CHEERING]
<v Na Dortch>第四幕，不要经过起点，不要收集200美元。有一段视频正在流传，我们很多人都看到了，我们认为在其中的作家金伯利·琼斯（Kimberly Jones）在给予背景和快速铺陈历史方面做得很好，以至于任何人都能理解。尽管这段视频在网上获得了很高的点击量，甚至在我们了解到约翰·奥利弗（John Oliver）上周结束他的HBO节目时播放了这段视频之后，我们仍然想在这里播放它。

00:57:41.120 --> 00:57:53.420
<v Dana Chivvis>I met up with Na a few days later in a park in Red Hook. When he walked up to me, he was talking to his team, saying maybe next he would run for some kind of elected position. Nothing too big, just something local.
<v Dana Chivvis>金伯利·琼斯以谈论最近抗议活动中的抢劫者开始了这段视频。她说，人们对抢劫者说了所有这些负面的话，但没问为什么他们要抢劫。为了解释很多人的一种感觉，她开始讲述美国黑人的经济史，从奴隶制开始。

00:57:53.420 --> 00:58:21.900
<v Na Dortch>Yesterday, I was in my house, and I was just laying down on my bed. And I'm like, wow. I really fucking did that. Black, queer man, broken tooth, a little chubby-- like, shit, I really did that. You know what I mean? It just feels like the odds are stacked against me. And I like winning. I like winning.
<v Na Dortch>我们绝不能忘记，经济是黑人被带到这个国家的原因。我们来南部做农业工作，在北部做纺织工作。你明白吗？这就是我们来做的事。

00:58:21.900 --> 00:58:28.530
<v Ira Glass>Dana Chivvis is one of the producers of our show.
<v Ira Glass>现在，如果我现在决定我想和你玩大富翁，在400轮大富翁游戏中，我不让你有任何钱，我不让你在棋盘上有任何东西，我不让你有任何东西。然后我们又玩了50轮大富翁，你在玩那轮大富翁时获得和赚取的一切都被拿走了——那是塔尔萨（Tulsa）。那是罗斯伍德（Rosewood）。

00:58:28.530 --> 00:58:55.210
<v Ira Glass>Act Four, Do Not Pass Go, Do Not Collect $200. So there's this video making the rounds that a bunch of us saw, and we thought the writer who is in it, Kimberly Jones, did such a good job giving context and laying out a history quickly in a way that anybody can understand. That even though this video has gotten a lot of views online and even after we learned that John Oliver ended his HBO show last week with this video, we still wanted to play it here.
<v Ira Glass>那些是我们建立黑人经济财富的地方，我们自给自足的地方，我们拥有商店的地方，我们拥有财产的地方，他们把它们烧成了平地。所以那是450年。所以400轮大富翁，你根本没机会玩。不仅你不能玩，你还得代表你正在与之对抗的那个人玩。你得玩，赚钱，为他们赚取财富，然后你得把它交给他们。

00:58:55.210 --> 00:59:12.090
<v Ira Glass>Kimberly Jones starts this video by talking about the looters in the recent protests. And she says, people say all these negative things about the looters, but don't ask why they're looting. And to explain a feeling that lots of people have, she launches into an economic history of black people in America, starting with slavery.
<v Ira Glass>所以50年来，你终于得到了一点点，你被允许玩了。每次他们不喜欢你玩的方式，或者你赶上来了，或者你在做自给自足的事，他们就烧掉你的游戏。他们烧掉你的牌。他们烧掉你的大富翁钱。

00:59:12.090 --> 00:59:27.040
<v Kimberly Jones>We must never forget that economics was the reason that black people were brought to this country. We came to do the agricultural work in the south and the textile work in the north. Do you understand that? That's what we came to do.
<v Kimberly Jones>然后，最后，在那之后，他们允许你玩，他们说，好吧，现在你赶上了。你怎么能赢？你怎么能赢？你不能赢。游戏是被操纵的。所以当他们说，为什么你烧毁了社区，为什么你烧毁了你自己的邻居，那不是我们的。我们什么都没有。我们什么都没有。

00:59:27.040 --> 00:59:53.370
<v Kimberly Jones>Now if I right now decided that I wanted to play Monopoly with you and for 400 rounds of playing Monopoly, I didn't allow you to have any money, I didn't allow you to have anything on the board, I didn't allow for you to have anything. And then we played another 50 rounds of Monopoly and everything that you gained and you earned while you were playing that round of Monopoly was taken from you-- that was Tulsa. That was Rosewood.
<v Kimberly Jones>特雷弗·诺亚（Trevor Noah）昨晚说得太美了。我们所有人都有一个社会契约。如果你们偷窃或如果我偷窃，那么作为权威的人就会介入，他们会解决问题。但解决问题的人正在杀我们！所以社会契约被打破了。

00:59:53.370 --> 01:00:22.530
<v Kimberly Jones>Those are places where we built black economic wealth, where we were self-sufficient, where we owned our stores, where we owned our property, and they burned them to the ground. So that's 450 years. So for 400 rounds of Monopoly, you don't get to play at all. Not only do you not get to play, you have to play on the behalf of the person that you're playing against. You have to play and make money and earn wealth for them, and then you have to turn it over to them.
<v Kimberly Jones>如果社会契约被打破了，为什么他妈的我还要在意烧毁该死的足球名人堂，烧毁该死的塔吉特（Target）？当你们在街上杀我们而且不在乎时，你们打破了契约！

01:00:22.530 --> 01:00:39.390
<v Kimberly Jones>So then for 50 years, you finally get a little bit, and you're allowed to play. And every time that they don't like the way that you're playing, or that you're catching up, or that you're doing something to be self-sufficient, they burn your game. They burn your cards. They burn your Monopoly money.
<v Kimberly Jones>你们打破了契约，400年来，我们玩了你们的游戏，建立了你们的财富。当我们在塔尔萨靠自己从零开始再次建立财富时，你们打破了契约，你们向我们投掷炸弹。当我们在罗斯伍德建立它时，你们进来屠杀了我们。

01:00:39.390 --> 01:01:08.560
<v Kimberly Jones>And then, finally, at the release and the onset of that, they allow you to play and they say, OK, now you catch up. How can you win? How can you win? You can't win. The game is fixed. So when they say, why did you burn down the community, why did you burn down your own neighborhood, it's not ours. We don't own anything. We don't own anything.
<v Kimberly Jones>你们打破了契约，所以去他妈的塔吉特。去他妈的名人堂。据我所知，他们可以把这个婊子烧成平地。那仍然不够。他们很幸运，黑人寻找的是平等，而不是复仇。

01:01:08.560 --> 01:01:27.510
<v Kimberly Jones>Trevor Noah said it so beautifully last night. There's a social contract that we all have. That if you steal or if I steal, then the person who is the authority comes in and they fix the situation. But the person who fixes the situation is killing us! So the social contract is broken.
<v Kimberly Jones>金伯利·琼斯，她是一位作家，一本青年小说的作者。她的网站是KimJonesWrites.com。

01:01:27.510 --> 01:01:40.710
<v Kimberly Jones>And if the social contract is broken, why the fuck do I give a shit about burning the fucking Football Hall of Fame, about burning a fucking Target? You broke the contract when you killed us in the streets and didn't give a fuck!
<v Kimberly Jones>[音乐 - Run The Jewels的《Walking in the Snow》]

01:01:40.710 --> 01:01:58.920
<v Kimberly Jones>You broke the contract, and for 400 years, we played your game and built your wealth. You broke the contract when we built our wealth again on our own by our bootstraps in Tulsa, and you dropped bombs on us. When we built it in Rosewood, and you came in and you slaughtered us.
<v Kimberly Jones>我们的节目今天由纳迪亚·雷曼（Nadia Reiman）和比姆·阿德温米（Bim Adewunmi）制作。制作今天节目的人包括伊曼纽尔·贝里（Emanuele Berry）、苏珊·伯顿（Susan Burton）、佐伊·蔡斯（Zoe Chace）、达娜·奇维斯（Dana Chivvis）、肖恩·科尔（Sean Cole）、阿维瓦·德科恩菲尔德（Aviva DeKornfeld）、努尔·吉尔（Noor Gill）、达米安·格拉夫（Damien Graef）、莉娜·米西齐斯（Lina Misitzis）、斯托·尼尔森（Stow Nelson）、凯瑟琳·雷·蒙多（Katharine Rae Mondo）、本·费兰（Ben Phelan）、罗宾·塞米恩（Robyn Semien）、阿丽莎·希普（Alissa Shipp）、莉莉·沙利文（Lilly Sullivan）、克里斯托弗·斯韦塔拉（Christopher Swetala）、马特·蒂尔尼（Matt Tierney）、南希·厄普代克（Nancy Updike）和朱莉·惠特克（Julie Whitaker）。

01:01:58.920 --> 01:02:21.060
<v Kimberly Jones>You broke the contract, so fuck your Target. Fuck your Hall of Fame. Far as I'm concerned, they could burn this bitch to the ground. And it still wouldn't be enough. And they are lucky that what black people are looking for is equality and not revenge.
